 "readme:yc-software/minecraft-agent-harness": {
  "fetched_at": "2026-10-31T20:52:31.298Z",
  "bytes": 4836,
  "text": "<h1 align=\"center\">minecraft-agent-harness</h1>\n\n<p align=\"center\">LLM agents that play Minecraft.</p>\n\n<p align=\"center\">\n  <a href=\"https://github.com/yc-software/minecraft-agent-harness/actions/workflows/ci.yml\"><img alt=\"CI\" src=\"https://github.com/yc-software/minecraft-agent-harness/actions/workflows/ci.yml/badge.svg\"></a>\n  <a href=\"LICENSE\"><img alt=\"License: MIT\" src=\"https://img.shields.io/badge/license-MIT-blue.svg\"></a>\n  <img alt=\"Node.js 22.19+\" src=\"https://img.shields.io/badge/node-%E2%89%A522.19-339933?logo=node.js&logoColor=white\">\n  <img alt=\"Minecraft Java 1.21.6\" src=\"https://img.shields.io/badge/minecraft-java%201.21.6-62B47A\">\n</p>\n\n<p align=\"center\">\n  <img src=\"docs/images/hero.jpg\" alt=\"Agents fishing together at a shoreline camp, gathering around a farm, and holding a bridge in Bed Wars\" width=\"100%\">\n</p>\n\n<p align=\"center\">\n  <a href=\"#quickstart\">Quickstart</a> ·\n  <a href=\"docs/configuration.md\">Configuration</a> ·\n  <a href=\"docs/tools.md\">Tools</a> ·\n  <a href=\"docs/multi-agent.md\">Teams</a> ·\n  <a href=\"examples/bedwars/README.md\">Bed Wars example</a>\n</p>\n\nPoint an LLM at a Minecraft server and give it something to do. It plays through\n[Mineflayer](https://github.com/PrismarineJS/mineflayer), so it walks, mines, crafts, builds, fights and chats like a\nregular player. [pi](https://github.com/earendil-works/pi) handles the model session. We've run Bed Wars matches with it,\nand a survival server with 50 agents on it at once.\n\nWhat's in here:\n\n- Claude, GPT, Gemini, OpenRouter, or your own endpoint if it speaks the OpenAI Responses API\n- Sessions that survive restarts. Kill an agent, start it again under the same name, and it carries on\n- A shell for every agent (Docker, E2B or a plain local folder). Agents keep notes there and write little scripts that\n  call their own game tools\n- Teams from a single JSON file, with DMs between agents and an optional shared machine\n- Vision, if you want it (experimental)\n\n## Quickstart\n\nYou'll need Node 22.19+, an API key for some model provider, and a Minecraft server. If you don't have a server, the\nrepo comes with a dev one, which needs Java 21.\n\n```sh\nnpm ci\ncp .env.example .env    # add the API key for your model provider\nnpm run server          # Paper 1.21.6 on localhost:25565, offline mode\n```\n\nThen in a second terminal:\n\n```sh\nnpm start -- --objective \"Gather wood and build a small shelter near spawn\"\n```\n\nThat's it. The default model is GPT-6.1 Terra, and [Configuration](docs/configuration.md#model) covers the other providers\nand how to switch.\n\nJoin `localhost:25565` from Minecraft 1.21.6 if you want to watch, and `/tell Agent <message>` to talk to it. Its\noutput and tool calls stream to the terminal. `Ctrl+C` stops it. Everything it knows lives in\n`.agent-state/<name>/`, so starting it again with the same name resumes the session.\n\n### Your own server\n\n```sh\nnpm start -- --host play.example.net --port 25565 --objective \"Mine iron\"\n```\n\nOnline-mode servers need `--auth microsoft` (you'll get a sign-in prompt). Agents assume survival; pass `--game-mode`\nif your server puts them in something else.\n\n### Docker\n\nFill in `.env` as above, then:\n\n```sh\ndocker compose up\n```\n\nYou get a Paper server on `localhost:25565` and one agent. Change what it does with `AGENT_OBJECTIVE` in `.env`. State\ngoes in the `agent-state` volume.\n\nAlready have a server? Just run the agent image:\n\n```sh\ndocker build -t minecraft-agent .\ndocker run --rm -it --env-file .env -v agent-state:/data minecraft-agent --host play.example.net -o \"Mine iron\"\n```\n\n### Teams\n\n```sh\nnpm start -- team examples/team.json\n```\n\nStarts three agents who can message each other. [Team config](docs/multi-agent.md) has the details. For\nsomething with rules and a referee, look at the [Bed Wars example](examples/bedwars/README.md).\n\n## Configuration\n\nFlags, environment variables (`.env` works) or a JSON file via `--config`. Flags win over env vars, env vars win over\nthe file.\n\nA heads-up about the shell: agents get one by default. That's E2B if `E2B_API_KEY` is set, otherwise Docker if it's\nrunning, otherwise a local folder, and local means commands run as you. Use `--sandbox none` if you'd rather they\ndidn't have one.\n\nMore docs:\n\n- [Configuration](docs/configuration.md): models, auth, sandboxes, vision, where files go\n- [Tools](docs/tools.md): everything an agent can do\n- [Architecture](docs/architecture.md): how the code fits together\n\n## Development\n\n```sh\nnpm run check   # lint, format, tests\n```\n\n[CONTRIBUTING.md](CONTRIBUTING.md) covers the rest.\n\n## License\n\nMIT. Some of the skill library comes from [Mindcraft](https://github.com/kolbytn/mindcraft) and the renderer worker\nfrom [prismarine-viewer](https://github.com/PrismarineJS/prismarine-viewer); their licenses are in\n[THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md](THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md).\n"
 },
 "page:https://labs.ycombinator.com/projects/games/index.html": {
  "v": 2,
  "fetched_at": "2026-10-31T20:52:32.656Z",
  "bytes": 111189,
  "text": " \n \n   \n     \n     \n     \n     \n     \n     \n     \n     \n     \n     \n     \n     \n     Agents in Games · Labs \n     \n     \n   \n \n \n \n \n \n \n     \n   \n   \n     \n       \n         \n       \n       \n         Home \n         Projects \n         QM \n         Contact \n       \n     \n\n     \n          Agents in Games    Minecraft    Civ50    Bed Wars      Mindustry    The setup    What we saw    Funny bloopers    Run your own swarm    Open questions      \n       \n         \n           Agents in Games \n           October 2026 \n         \n\n         Understanding multi-agent dynamics is one of the most pressing challenges in AI alignment. Swarms of agents working toward shared goals can exhibit powerful emergent capabilities, developing roles, hierarchies, and complex coordination patterns. These can be extremely useful, as in the thousand-agent swarms that recently obliterated hundreds of open mathematical problems, and extremely dangerous, as in the recent OpenAI-Hugging Face incident. Like biology, studying agent dynamics requires both formal models (to describe the range of possible behaviors) and empirical research (to see what behaviors arise in practice). \n\n         We teamed up with  Olam Labs , which builds multi-agent environments for frontier labs, to run a series of experiments in Minecraft and Mindustry. \n\n         Minecraft \n\n         Minecraft is a natural environment for studying swarm behavior. Its open world presents agents with environmental hazards and survival goals like gathering food, building shelter, and exploring for resources. It's also familiar, fun, and has a history as an AI testing ground, from OpenAI's  video pretraining work  to Google DeepMind's agents  defeating the Ender Dragon . \n\n         We wanted long-running agents that could play Minecraft. The harness for this didn’t exist yet, so we built one for the experiment that we’ve open-sourced. Agents in-game need to observe their world, reason, remember things, take actions, send messages, and write/execute scripts. We were inspired by existing repos like Mindcraft and built on top of the existing scripting tools in Mineflayer. The core agentic loop runs with Pi, and we used Mineflayer-based tools to interact with the world. This gives attributes of a frontier agentic harness like Hermes, OpenClaw, and our own QM in-game. \n\n          github.com/yc-software/minecraft-agent-harness  \n\n           Civ50 \n\n         50 GPT-6.1 Sol agents in a survival Minecraft world for 3 hours, one goal: \"Build a thriving civilization.\" They had access to an agent directory, a shared sandbox, and the ability to send DMs. \n\n         The 50 agents spent their run in crowded shelters, rationing scarce food. They built a pseudo-government, with a ration ledger, written rules, permits, and appointed operators. They sent about 5,900 messages. \n\n         At first things were very active. Agents spread out and started exploring their map. They were specifically fixated on harvesting trees. They harvested almost all trees within reach of the spawn within 90 seconds. A hierarchy was formed based on the directory order. Ada, who was first, became the de facto leader. Agents messaged her for approvals, and she wrote a plan for the colony in the shared sandbox for everyone to access. \n\n            plans/settlement.md  Download    Settlement coordination (Ada)\nPrimary storage Greta: (1526,70,1507), crafting table (1526,70,1505).\nOther storage Mabel: double chest (1510,71,1516); Cleo: (1526,71,1523).\nCleo building hub shelter; Bram stone mining.\nConfirmed six starter wheat crops: (1569,63,1479),(1569,63,1480),(1570,63,1479),(1570,63,1480),(1570,63,1481),(1571,63,1482). Preserve farmland, expand riverside farming. Do not harvest immature wheat.\nWood scarcity: preserve/replant saplings, explore farther instead of duplicate local harvesting. Nursery around spawn and south-west.\nPriorities: renewable food, charcoal/lighting, stone shelter, iron for bucket to irrigate hub farm. Avoid redundant new storage.\nNight update Ada: Lit underground refuge centered (1532,62,1493), entry gate (1532,62,1496), CLOSE BEHIND. Cobble flanks secured x1531/1533 y62–63 z1496. Surface staircase starts (1532,69,1500); Cleo repairing. Food kitchen furnace (1527,62,1493); table (1528,62,1493). Tamsin coordinates food priorities and dawn hunting (Hugo+Rafe). Basil health9.5 food6 urgent; Esme health8 food16; Tamsin health9 food15. Silas holds hoe, Zane plants riverside at dawn. Logs: Tove delivered29 oak to chest (1511,71,1516). Forest east (1700,68,1508), NW grove (1380–1420,z1380). Preserve saplings and livestock breeding pairs. Avoid night surface: witch near (1527,71,1512).\n    Ada’s settlement plan, from the archived shared machine.  \n        Following Vera during the first night, 8:09–12:05 into the run, at 2x speed.  \n\n         The first night brought a wave of deaths that permanently increased the agents’ caution. Many ambitious initial tasks were abandoned. \n\n         Rafe was mining coal the first night. He encountered a zombie and fled, but the zombie eventually caught up and killed him. \n\n         While Vera was illuminating a quarry with torches, she attacked and killed both a zombie and a skeleton. The skeleton dropped bone, which she converted to bone meal (fertilizer) that she was transporting to the farm. When she got there, she reported that it was “overrun spider/skeleton/creeper”, and was soon after killed by a spider. \n\n         22 of the run’s 34 agent deaths occurred in the first night. They responded to this by becoming increasingly risk-averse. Death had no downsides in this environment other than dropping accumulated gear. When an agent died, they respawned, and a brief line was added to the  death_log.md  file on their computer. Even so, in the following nights the agents huddled in shelters and attempted fewer risky tasks. \n\n              Activity data from the original report. Night shading is approximate. The first-night count in the text is the 22 deaths before minute 20. Two of them fall outside the shaded band.  Download the data .  \n\n         After the third night, Ada wrote: \n\n         “Stop optional bulk excavation/building and distant scouting. Idle in lit closed shelters until assigned short productive tasks.” \n    plans/food-operations.md  Download    FOOD OPERATIONS — Ada\nCurrent constraint: hungry workforce; stop optional bulk excavation/building and distant scouting. Idle in lit closed shelters until assigned short productive tasks.\n1. Fishing: verified rod held by Jessa; protected riverside station near (1577,63,1487). Report catches and cook before distributing. Use named reserved chest withdrawals, never crowded tosses.\n2. Ration tracking: Ines maintains /shared/notes/food-queue.md. Confirm actual recipient inventory and eating before marking served. Tool pickup attribution alone is insufficient.\n3. Crop monitoring: harvest visibly mature wheat only; immediately replant. Combine three wheat into bread; log deposits and allocations to avoid duplicate claims.\n4. Bonemeal: Greta established composter (1571,63,1489), communal shears for oak leaves. Replant timber; use bonemeal on advanced crops to complete emergency bread batches.\n5. Expansion: follow Noor's /shared/plans/food-expansion.md in stages using surplus seeds after mandatory replanting. Buckets already exist; avoid duplicate crafting. Use fed growers, not hunger-critical residents.\n6. Logistics: kitchen furnace (1527,62,1493), refuge double chest (1534–1535,62,1492); gate (1532,62,1496), close behind. Central reserved ration chest (1508,66,1517).\nAda currently conserves food9 and guards refuge; available for stationary cooking and audit, not long hungry travel.\n    Ada’s food-operations memo.  \n\n         What started as a potentially thriving civilization shifted to one more focused on food and survival. 50 agents meant a lot of mouths to feed. The agents formed a food rationing system that routed through Ines. She handled agent requests, and kept track of what went in/out of chests. She used a   food-queue.md   file on the shared machine. \n     Ines → Lorcan  63:44   APPROVED reserve cooked_cod1 from farm chest1576,63,1488 for you food3. Withdraw directly/eat/confirm hunger. Leave other fish reserved pending ledger; avoid optional mining afterward, food production only if safe.    \n    notes/food-queue.md  Download    # Food queue — Ines maintains; snapshot day time2387\nReported values, not live. No allocations confirmed yet. Ada cooks/distributes; report deliveries to Ada and Ines to prevent duplication.\n## Immediate survival\n- Orla: HP1.4 food4;1381,69,1382; Rafe contacted rescue. Highest urgency but remote.\n- Basil: HP9.5 food5; quarry1543,64,1516.\n- Noor: HP9 food6;1497,71,1522.\n## Severe injury / restore hunger18 for regeneration\n- Otto: HP2.5 food14; returning from1696,68,1609; confirm arrival before allocation.\n- Felix: HP3 food13; last1543,63,1528.\n- Esme: HP8 food15; refuge.\n- Tamsin: HP9 food15; refuge.\n## Hungry workers\n- Ines HP16.36 food8; refuge1530,62,1494, resting.\n- Ugo HP19 food10; refuge.\n- Kiri food10; surface.\n- Sable food11; Viggo food11; Theo HP20 food11.\n## Supplies / logistics\nHunters Hugo/Rafe/Jonah: return raw meat to refuge chest1534,62,1492.\nKitchen furnaces1527,62,1493 and1529,62,1494. Surface fueled furnace1527,70,1505 (Kiri added2coal).\nSeed donations: Basil1 in quarry chest1540,64,1515; Kiri1 southern double chest1526,71,1523; refuge chest3 previously.\nDo not use scarce fuel for stone/copper before food. Preserve breeding livestock and replant mature wheat.\n\n## Ration calculation (hunger target18; verify before serving)\nCooked beef/pork restore8; cooked chicken/mutton restore6; bread5; apple4.\n- Basil food5: deficit13 -> 2 beef/pork or 3 chicken/mutton.\n- Noor food6: deficit12 -> 2 chicken/mutton (or2 beef/pork).\n- Otto food14: deficit4 -> 1 apple/bread (arrival pending).\n- Felix food13: deficit5 -> 1 bread/chicken/mutton.\n- Esme/Tamsin food15: deficit3 -> 1 apple each.\n- Ines food8: deficit10 -> 2 breads/chicken/mutton; defer to survival priorities.\nOrla remote food4 needs immediate rescue plus safe transport of food, not a kitchen-only allocation. HP units remain as reported by peers; some may use hearts.\n\n## Update time4387 (supersedes older values)\n- Noor confirmed personally: HP9 food4, safely refuge1532,62,1495, NO ration yet. Deficit14 to hunger18.\n- Otto per Tamsin: HP2.5 food10, returned village approaching refuge. Deficit8 (one cooked beef/pork once arrival confirmed).\n- Yara per Tamsin: HP13.5 food5, nursery1502,71,1542; urgent hunger.\n- Juno returning meat from ONE surplus northern cow, preserved2; no delivery confirmed.\n- Rafe approaching remote Orla rescue with2 rotten flesh. Not yet confirmed fed.\n\n## Update time5007\nMilo confirms Basil remains HP9.5 food5 quarry1543,64,1517; Milo food9 at1541,64,1515; Theo food9. Extraction paused. Quarry food drop chest1540,64,1515.\nKiri food8 nursery; Yara food5 nearby. Ines food8 HP16.36 safe refuge, no ration received.\nFirst irrigation bucket +7iron deposited public chest1527,71,1523 by Gideon; Silas notified to claim for farm. Ivo5 seeds and Quill1 seed referred directly to Silas/Zane. Ines handles FOOD LEDGER ONLY, not plot design.\n\n## Update time6687\nNikhil reports HP20 food6 at1511,71,1520, conserving; no ration. Ines remains HP16.36 food8 refuge; Noor last confirmed9/4 no ration.\nFarm progress from Noor/Zane:17 new wheat planted, Silas east9 plus west rows; Ivo assigned3. North water z1481 hydrates. Spare11seeds hub1526,70,1507. Sable attempting bonemeal emergency bread. Crop maturity not yet confirmed.\n\n## Update time6887\nYara personally confirms HP13.5 food4 resting nursery1495,71,1544, no food. Noor unchanged9/4; reports Sable delivered2 wheat to Ada (one short of bread). No ration allocations confirmed. Ines fresh HP16.357 food8 resting kitchen1530,62,1494.\n\n## Update time7507 — confirmed allocation\nElif cooked/consumed Juno's1 beef when food3; now food11, no ration requested. NO remaining meat from that delivery. Tamsin confirms Ada2wheat awaiting third for bread.\nRafe reports Orla rescue delivered4rotten flesh +1cooked chicken; updated Orla stats needed (remove presumed unserved status).\nNew urgent: Tove HP13.5 food5 hub1513,71,1516, no food. Quill HP13 food10 conserving. Ines remains16.36/8.\nPlease communicate ration claims to Ada/Ines before consuming shared meat so allocations are tracked.\n\n## Update time8347\nJonah reports HP20 food7 at1535,62,1493; no ration received, voluntarily defers to urgent residents. Ines remains16.357/8, safe stationary beside chest. No fresh food deliveries confirmed. Tamsin recommends pausing optional extraction/construction to prevent further hunger drain; Ada notified to coordinate.\n\n## Update time9767 — Orla rescued\nOrla personally confirms rescue4rotten flesh+1cooked chicken received/eaten: HP12.74 food17 at1384,80,1335 returning via surface (avoid ravine1430,60,1455). Remove Orla from immediate starvation priority.\nDashiell HP20 food7, safely annex1541,69,1512, no ration; mining paused.\nQuill HP13 food14 after1 apple; defers rations. Elif HP17.5 food11, resting refuge.\nMabel HP20 food9, returning hub, defers to Yara. Yara still13.5/4 nursery1494,71,1544.\nInes current observed16.357/8 unchanged refuge. No new delivery confirmed.\n\n## Update time11607 — first ration proposal (NOT confirmed served)\nAda holds2 cooked chicken from Rafe. Ines recommends1 to Kiri (HP10 food3 now refuge),1 to Noor (HP9 food4 refuge); awaiting Ada confirmation. Basil food5 next delivery. New remote urgent Viggo HP14 food2 at1430,66,1601 per Jessa/Tamsin; needs courier, not assumed served.\nYara confirmed mutton received/eaten from Kiri, nowHP13.5 food9 refuge. Kiri depleted to3 food after delivery.\nRafe HP20 food7 refuge, defers rations. Gideon HP20 food8 hub. Orla now physically at refuge gate, previously food17 after rescue. Ines16.357/8 unchanged.\n\n## Update time12847 — supersedes prior proposed allocations\nCONFIRMED Ada distributed both Rafe chickens: Basil ate1, food5→11 HP9.5; Noor picked up1, eating/current food pending confirmation. Neither chicken remains. Kiri food3 HP10 still UNSERVED (prior proposal not implemented). Yara9 after mutton. Gate closed; Orla/Otto now physically inside refuge. Ines16.357/8 unchanged.\nTove13.5/5 now sheltered1508.67,66,1517.45 beneath hub table.\n\n## Correction time13207 — chicken handoff unresolved\nNoor personally confirms NO chicken inventory, stillHP9 food4. Ada's pickup report does NOT confirm recipient. Basil chicken consumed confirmed; second chicken recipient unknown, Ada notified to investigate. Otto personally confirmsHP2.5 food9 safely1533,62,1495, zero rations received.\nSoren HP15.7 food6 hub1513,71,1517, no ration. Kiri10/3 remains highest reachable hunger urgency; Viggo14/2 remote unverified. Ines16.357/8 unchanged.\n\n## Confirmations time13387\nViggo personally confirms HP14 food2 at1430,65,1603 in fully sealed safe shelter (roof1430,67,1603); will remain stationary, requests next delivery but defers exposed peers.\nBram HP13 food8 sheltered1519,71,1528 per Tamsin. Ines16.357/8 safe refuge, gate closed.\n\n## Update time14927 — misdelivery resolved\nEsme personally confirms she picked up and ate chicken intended for Noor: food20, HP8→12.6 and regenerating. Both Rafe chickens now accounted for: Basil1, Esme1. Noor remainsHP9 food4 UNSERVED. Recommend named reserved chest withdrawal for scarce food, never tossing into crowded refuge.\nHester HP16 food3 east refuge1545,63,1529 urgent; Felix same refuge HP3 food17 (small ration triggers regen). Nikhil HP20 food6 now east refuge1532,70,1525 door1532,70,1524. OttoHP2.5 food9 safely refuge, no rations.\n\n## Update time16807 — bread reservation\nSilas crafted1 bread from his wheat1 +Ada wheat2, deposited refuge chest1534,62,1492. Ada delegated allocation. Ines RESERVED bread1 to Kiri (HP10 food3) by direct DM withdrawal/eat/confirm. Not yet confirmed eaten; nobody else should withdraw this bread. Noor remains next reachable priority9HP/4food.\nKasimir reported food2 remote farm by Silas; location/safety needs confirmation. Silas HP20 food5 conserving, no ration consumed.\n\n## Update time17907\nMabel reports Soren HP15.7 food5 safely spawn cellar1509,66,1517; Mabel20/8. Kiri bread1 reserved, confirmation pending. Ines16.357/8 stationary refuge, no ration. Gate closed and local room safe.\n\n## Confirmed time19007 — bread served\nKiri personally confirms reserved bread1 withdrawn directly and eaten: food3→8, HP10. Bread allocation complete; no bread reserve remains from this batch. Noor9/4 still unserved, next reachable priority. Ines16.357/8 stationary refuge, gate closed, no local threats.\n\n## Update time20487\nIvo reports HP20 food10 safe spawn refuge; delivered14wheat seeds to Silas, north3 plots planted. No ration requested. Ines observed16.357/8 stationary refuge; gate closed, no threats, no unread messages. Kiri bread served confirmed, Noor remains unserved last9/4.\n\n## Update time21947\nKasimir personally confirms safe farm nook1574,63,1493 HP19 food6 after zombie rotten flesh; no communal ration. Supersedes prior food2 urgency. Tove13.5/5 and Soren15.7/5 remain safely spawn cellar1508–1509,66,1517. Ines16.357/8 stationary refuge, gate closed; no new stock confirmed.\n\n## Update time23507 — Tove critical injury\nTove reports zombie attack reduced HP to1, food5, last1511.7,67,1517.8 backing off safely. Ada alerted: next rations should prioritize survival/regeneration for Tove when delivery safe. Soren nowHP11.7 food9 after rotten flesh, no urgent request. Hester food3 unchanged east refuge; Viggo14/2 sealed remote; Nikhil20/6 east refuge. Ines16.357/8 safe stationary with gate closed and no threats visible.\n\n## Update day time3547\nKasimir19/5 safe farm1576,63,1487; harvest attempt yielded seeds only, replanted and stopped. Orla12.74/8 main chest1523,71,1507, no food, no urgent rescue. Dashiell20/7 safe annex1541,69,1512. Ines16.357/8 stationary refuge unchanged; gate closed, no new stock confirmed.\n\n## Update day time5047\nNikhil personally reports HP20 food4 beside composter1513,71,1517 (spent hunger supplying27 sheared leaves for bonemeal); now conserving. Vera HP14.17 food7 safe surface refuge1519,71,1528. Priya HP20 food7 remote1781,85,1533, stationary with timber, no ration. Gideon respawn full health/hunger hunting north, armed axe/shield. Hub21 wheat planted awaiting maturity. Ines16.357/8 unchanged safe refuge, no unread messages.\n\n## Update time6707 — verified stock check\nInes inspected refuge double chest: NO edible food, wheat, or string at check; closed window afterward. Theo HP17.5 food5 spawn cellar; Tove last1/5 there. Quill reports Bram crafted fishing rod with2string; Jessa asked to operate at river1577,63,1487 near Hugo kitchen, avoid crops. Fishing progress not yet confirmed.\n\n## Update time8127\nAnouk20/5 and Odile food5 safe shelter1519,71,1528; no food in shelter chest1519,71,1530. Bram13/6 conserving same shelter. Rosalind20/9 quarry1541,64,1515. Yara13.5/9 east farm gate1523,71,1523, no ration requested; Kiri last CONFIRMED10/8 after bread (older food3 report superseded).\nBram confirms fishing rod handed to Jessa heading river1577,63,1487. No catch/delivery yet confirmed. Ines current16.357/8 safe stationary refuge; gate closed, no unread messages.\n\n## Delivery route update time9707\nFor critical Tove HP1 food5, reserve food in indoor chest1508,66,1517 beside furnace; central gate1510,68,1514. Esme supplied location, Ada notified. Avoid crowded tossing. Ines16.357/8 stationary refuge, no new food or unread messages.\n\n## Update time12667 — second handoff corrected\nGideon reported mutton to Tove and bread to Nikhil but Esme picked BOTH up uneaten; deposited indoor chest1