nal supports two android devices in one account as standard \n\n             \n     \n      \n      \n    \n     \n         \n                 resposta  \n                     \n         \n            \n \n          \n \n -1 \n \n          \n \n\n         \n         \n            \n         \n         \n                \n             \n         \n             \n         \n             \n                 \n                       \n                 \n                 \n                      \n                 \n             \n         \n     \n      \n     \n            \n                            \n \n     \n         \n             by \n             \n \n             \n            exdor @programming.dev \n         \n         \n         \n         \n\n              \n                 6 hours ago \n                    profunditat: 4 \n             \n         \n                \n         \n     \n\n     \n         \n             Yeah, since a month or so, and emphasis on 2 and not unlimited \n\n             \n     \n      \n      \n    \n     \n         \n                 resposta  \n                     \n         \n            \n \n          \n \n 3 \n \n          \n \n\n         \n         \n            \n         \n         \n                \n             \n         \n             \n         \n             \n                 \n                       \n                 \n                 \n                      \n                 \n             \n         \n     \n      \n     \n \n                        \n                    \n                            \n \n     \n         \n             by \n             \n \n            wunderkatze @discuss.tchncs.de \n         \n         \n         \n         \n\n              \n                 11 hours ago \n                    profunditat: 4 \n             \n         \n                \n         \n     \n\n     \n         \n             Really? That’s new to me… I’ll check it out \n\n             \n     \n      \n      \n    \n     \n         \n                 resposta  \n                     \n         \n            \n \n          \n \n 2 \n \n          \n \n\n         \n         \n            \n         \n         \n                \n             \n         \n             \n         \n             \n                 \n                       \n                 \n                 \n                      \n                 \n             \n         \n     \n      \n     \n \n                        \n                     \n     \n \n                        \n                     \n     \n \n                        \n                    \n                            \n \n     \n         \n             by \n             \n \n             \n            razen @lemmy.world \n         \n         \n         \n         \n\n              \n                 11 hours ago \n                    profunditat: 2 \n             \n         \n                \n         \n     \n\n     \n         \n             Signal is distributed by the Guardian Project on Fdroid.  \n\n             \n     \n      \n      \n    \n     \n         \n                 resposta  \n                     \n         \n            \n \n          \n \n 2 \n \n          \n \n\n         \n         \n            \n         \n         \n                \n             \n         \n             \n         \n             \n                 \n                       \n                 \n                 \n                      \n                 \n             \n         \n     \n      \n     \n            \n                            \n \n     \n         \n             by \n             \n \n             \n            exdor @programming.dev \n         \n         \n         \n         \n\n              \n                 6 hours ago \n                    profunditat: 3 \n             \n         \n                \n         \n     \n\n     \n         \n             Yeah unofficially… that is very much a bandaid. It is really bad of Signal to not have a blobfree reproducible build on F-Droid and Flathub, or even just external repos (for F-Droid and flathub). \n Instead they have a hidden self-updating APK (which is a very cursed concept) with blobs, and a damn Appimage on Linux. \n\n             \n     \n      \n      \n    \n     \n         \n                 resposta  \n                     \n         \n            \n \n          \n \n 1 \n \n          \n \n\n         \n         \n            \n         \n         \n                \n             \n         \n             \n         \n             \n                 \n                       \n                 \n                 \n                      \n                 \n             \n         \n     \n      \n     \n            \n                            \n \n     \n         \n             by \n             \n \n             \n            razen @lemmy.world \n         \n         \n         \n         \n\n              \n                Editat  4 hours ago \n                    profunditat: 4 \n             \n         \n                \n         \n     \n\n     \n         \n             Yeah,  is there any actual reason given by Signal for this?  \n\n             \n     \n      \n      \n    \n     \n         \n                 resposta  \n                     \n         \n            \n \n          \n \n 1 \n \n          \n \n\n         \n         \n            \n         \n         \n                \n             \n         \n             \n         \n             \n                 \n                       \n                 \n                 \n                      \n                 \n             \n         \n     \n      \n     \n \n                        \n                     \n     \n \n                        \n                     \n     \n \n                        \n                    \n                            \n \n     \n         \n             by \n             \n \n            nelson @lemmy.world \n         \n         \n         \n         \n\n              \n                 2 hours ago \n                    profunditat: 2 \n             \n         \n                \n         \n     \n\n     \n         \n             It does some extra stuff signal doesn’t ( apparently).\nThough there’s always a risk using a 3rd party client. And I guess it might be against the TOS of signal? \n \n encrypt the database with a password \n not using google for notifications \n ram shedding\nAnd some others…. \n \n  https://molly.im/  \n\n             \n     \n      \n      \n    \n     \n         \n                 resposta  \n                     \n         \n            \n \n          \n \n 1 \n \n          \n \n\n         \n         \n            \n         \n         \n                \n             \n         \n             \n         \n             \n                 \n                       \n                 \n                 \n                      \n                 \n             \n         \n     \n      \n     \n \n                        \n                    \n                            \n \n     \n         \n             by \n             \n \n            BillionaireStew @lemmy.world \n         \n         \n         \n         \n\n              \n                 8 hours ago \n                    profunditat: 2 \n             \n         \n                \n         \n     \n\n     \n         \n             Why run Signal when  Session  is right there? Maybe you just like leaking metadata? \n  https://abcnews.com/blogs/headlines/2014/05/ex-nsa-chief-we-kill-people-based-on-metadata/  \n\n             \n     \n      \n      \n    \n     \n         \n                 resposta  \n                     \n         \n            \n \n          \n \n -1 \n \n          \n \n\n         \n         \n            \n         \n         \n                \n             \n         \n             \n         \n             \n                 \n                       \n                 \n                 \n                      \n                 \n             \n         \n     \n      \n     \n            \n                            \n \n     \n         \n             by \n             \n \n             \n            exdor @programming.dev \n         \n         \n         \n         \n\n              \n                 6 hours ago \n                    profunditat: 3 \n             \n         \n                \n         \n     \n\n     \n         \n             Session has removed perfect forward secrecy. I dont know if they still have broken autodeletion and still store all messages in a blockchain. Overall though, I would stay away from it. \n\n             \n     \n      \n      \n    \n     \n         \n                 resposta  \n                     \n         \n            \n \n          \n \n 2 \n \n          \n \n\n         \n         \n            \n         \n         \n                \n             \n         \n             \n         \n             \n                 \n                       \n                 \n                 \n                      \n                 \n             \n         \n     \n      \n     \n \n                        \n                     \n     \n \n                        \n                     \n     \n \n              \n            \n                  \n \n     \n         \n             by \n             \n \n             \n            exdor @programming.dev \n         \n         \n         \n         \n\n              \n                Editat  6 hours ago \n                    profunditat: 1 \n             \n         \n                \n         \n     \n\n     \n         \n             Signal-FOSS as alternative \n I use Signal-FOSS by twinhelix. It exists since many years and upatches are fully automated. \n They are very simple, deblob signal, remove firebase messages and maps and whatnot. \n Twinhelix has also added some of the  jw patches , which are nice to have. \n It does not \n \n remove donations (which is nice and kinda shit of molly) \n remove payments with mobilecoin (kinda useless sadly as very few exchanges support it) \n add blobfree firebase messaging \n add unifiedpush support \n support linking multiple phones \n support encrypting the database \n probably more \n \n If you dont need those features, I   highly   recommend it. Signal shipping Google blobs and having no F-Droid repo is very bad and that shouldn’t be supported.  \n  See the list of known 3rd party F-Droid repos  \n UnifiedPush issues \n Note that UnifiedPush needs to be supported by the server. The server then sends the push message to a UnifiedPush  distributor  (like Conversations, ntfy or Sunup). That distributor wakes up the app, which sends you the notification. \n There is a slight polling delay of about 1 minute, so notifications are delayed. \n I measured the effect of this by comparing molly with UP and the Signal APK with websocket. On a Pixel 8a running GrapheneOS, 12 hours idle on Wifi, airplane mode on (as the modem uses  by far  the most battery). I configured to send 10 messages to the device using Signals “send later” feature. \n Websocket used 3% of the batterylife. Thats it. \n And that effect is only significant for people who rarely use Signal, so the likelyhood of a nerd configuring MollySocket falling into that category is pretty low. If you regularly open Signal, this only delays notification alerts for no benefit. \n And because the Signal servers   don’t officially support this   you need to either selfhost MollySocket (which would be fine apart from potential update delays, what this post is about) or trust some server operator. MollySocket is registered as another device, so the Signal servers and any standard Signal client would treat it as a trusted device with its own decryption key.  \n Apparently MollySocket discards the key and only receives “you have a message” (and no other metadata? I have obviously not researched this a lot), and I suppose Molly ensures that the device will never get a decryption key either. Still, it increases attack surface for very limited benefit. \n It would be great if Signal officially supported UP instead of Google FCM. \n\n             \n     \n      \n      \n    \n     \n         \n                 resposta  \n                     \n         \n            \n \n          \n \n 5 \n \n          \n \n\n         \n         \n            \n         \n         \n                \n             \n         \n             \n         \n             \n                 \n                       \n                 \n                 \n                      \n                 \n             \n         \n     \n      \n     \n \n              \n            \n                  \n \n     \n         \n             by \n             \n \n            vatlark @lemmy.world \n         \n         \n         \n         \n\n              \n                 12 hours ago \n                    profunditat: 1 \n             \n         \n                \n         \n     \n\n     \n         \n             Aww bummer \n\n             \n     \n      \n      \n    \n     \n         \n                 resposta  \n                     \n         \n            \n \n          \n \n 4 \n \n          \n \n\n         \n         \n            \n         \n         \n                \n             \n         \n             \n         \n             \n                 \n                       \n                 \n                 \n                      \n                 \n             \n         \n     \n      \n     \n \n              \n            \n                  \n \n     \n         \n             by \n             \n \n             \n            inari @kbin.earth \n         \n         \n         \n           \n         \n\n              \n                Editat  11 hours ago \n                    profunditat: 1 \n             \n         \n                \n         \n     \n\n     \n         \n             That sucks. Does the original Signal app deliver notifications properly without Play Services?  \n\n             \n     \n      \n      \n    \n     \n         \n                 resposta  \n                     \n         \n            \n \n          \n \n 4 \n \n          \n \n\n         \n         \n            \n         \n         \n                \n             \n         \n             \n         \n             \n                 \n                       \n                 \n                 \n                      \n                 \n             \n         \n     \n      \n     \n            \n                            \n \n     \n         \n             by \n             \n \n             \n            doodeux @scribe.disroot.org \n         \n         \n         \n         \n\n              \n                 11 hours ago \n                    profunditat: 2 \n             \n         \n                \n         \n     \n\n     \n         \n             I’m new to GrapheneOS and running Signal without anything configured with the word Google in it.  I am receiving notifications just fine.  \n\n             \n     \n      \n      \n    \n     \n         \n                 resposta  \n                     \n         \n            \n \n          \n \n 7 \n \n          \n \n\n         \n         \n            \n         \n         \n                \n             \n         \n             \n         \n             \n                 \n                       \n                 \n                 \n                      \n                 \n             \n         \n     \n      \n     \n            \n                            \n \n     \n         \n             by \n             \n \n             \n            exdor @programming.dev \n         \n         \n         \n         \n\n              \n                Editat  6 hours ago \n                    profunditat: 3 \n             \n         \n                \n         \n     \n\n     \n         \n             That depends on where you got the APK from \n \n the playstore apk only supports FCM \n the standalone, hidden (you only find it via search engines), apk on their website also supports websocket \n Twinhelix Signal-FOSS only supports websocket \n molly also supports blobfree FCM and UnifiedPush \n \n But note that UnifiedPush is not supported by signal, so you need to register a fake device on a server running MollySocket. Which is very much additional attack surface and only worth it if you really rarely use signal \n\n             \n     \n      \n      \n    \n     \n         \n                 resposta  \n                     \n         \n            \n \n          \n \n 0 \n \n          \n \n\n         \n         \n            \n         \n         \n                \n             \n         \n             \n         \n             \n                 \n                       \n                 \n                 \n                      \n                 \n             \n         \n     \n      \n     \n \n                        \n                     \n     \n \n                        \n                    \n                            \n \n     \n         \n             by \n             \n \n             \n            BurgerBaron @quokk.au \n         \n         \n         \n         \n he/him \n              \n                 8 hours ago \n                    profunditat: 2 \n             \n         \n                \n         \n     \n\n     \n         \n             The APK from Signal’s website doesn’t require Play services, just don’t install Signal via Play Store. DaNgEr ZoNE eye rolls aside: \n  https://signal.org/android/apk  \n Annoying, I rather liked Molly. \n\n             \n     \n      \n      \n    \n     \n         \n                 resposta  \n                     \n         \n            \n \n          \n \n 3 \n \n          \n \n\n         \n         \n            \n         \n         \n                \n             \n         \n             \n         \n             \n                 \n                       \n                 \n                 \n                      \n                 \n             \n         \n     \n      \n     \n            \n                            \n \n     \n         \n             by \n             \n \n             \n            exdor @programming.dev \n         \n         \n         \n         \n\n              \n                 6 hours ago \n                    profunditat: 3 \n             \n         \n                \n         \n     \n\n     \n         \n             Use Verified-Apps from PrivacyGuides to verify the signature of the APK before installing. \n Before Appverifier was a thing, it was very obscure how to even check that signature. \n\n             \n     \n      \n      \n    \n     \n         \n                 resposta  \n                     \n         \n            \n \n          \n \n 2 \n \n          \n \n\n         \n         \n            \n         \n         \n                \n             \n         \n             \n         \n             \n                 \n                       \n                 \n                 \n                      \n                 \n             \n         \n     \n      \n     \n            \n                            \n \n     \n         \n             by \n             \n \n             \n            BurgerBaron @quokk.au \n         \n         \n         \n         \n he/him \n              \n                 6 hours ago \n                    profunditat: 4 \n             \n         \n                \n         \n     \n\n     \n         \n             I’m going go try Signal-FOSS instead that you mentioned earlier. \n\n             \n     \n      \n      \n    \n     \n         \n                 resposta  \n                     \n         \n            \n \n          \n \n 1 \n \n          \n \n\n         \n         \n            \n         \n         \n                \n             \n         \n             \n         \n             \n                 \n                       \n                 \n                 \n                      \n                 \n             \n         \n     \n      \n     \n \n                        \n                     \n     \n \n                        \n                     \n     \n \n                        \n                    \n                            \n \n     \n         \n             by \n             \n \n            bad1080 @piefed.social \n         \n         \n         \n         \n\n              \n                Editat  11 hours ago \n                    profunditat: 2 \n             \n         \n                \n         \n     \n\n     \n         \n             i have no problems with notifications on crdroid (lineageOS fork) and microG \n\n             \n     \n      \n      \n    \n     \n         \n                 resposta  \n                     \n         \n            \n \n          \n \n 1 \n \n          \n \n\n         \n         \n            \n         \n         \n                \n             \n         \n             \n         \n             \n                 \n                       \n                 \n                 \n                      \n                 \n             \n         \n     \n      \n     \n            \n                            \n \n     \n         \n             by \n             \n \n             \n            brvslvrnst @lemmy.ml \n         \n         \n         \n         \n\n              \n                 9 hours ago \n                    profunditat: 3 \n             \n         \n                \n         \n     \n\n     \n         \n             Iirc, the push notifications are flowing through Google firebase, which is why you still get them. \n\n             \n     \n      \n      \n    \n     \n         \n                 resposta  \n                     \n         \n            \n \n          \n \n 2 \n \n          \n \n\n        