name\":\"Zhongpeng Cai\",\"hidden\":false},{\"_id\":\"6ae45f48c3b566b041f6ca81\",\"name\":\"Qing Zhou\",\"hidden\":false},{\"_id\":\"6ae45f48c3b566b041f6ca82\",\"name\":\"Zekai Zhang\",\"hidden\":false},{\"_id\":\"6ae45f48c3b566b041f6ca83\",\"name\":\"Kun Zhang\",\"hidden\":false},{\"_id\":\"6ae45f48c3b566b041f6ca84\",\"name\":\"Zezhong Wu\",\"hidden\":false},{\"_id\":\"6ae45f48c3b566b041f6ca85\",\"name\":\"Jian Hu\",\"hidden\":false},{\"_id\":\"6ae45f48c3b566b041f6ca86\",\"name\":\"Haihan Gao\",\"hidden\":false},{\"_id\":\"6ae45f48c3b566b041f6ca87\",\"name\":\"Heting Gao\",\"hidden\":false},{\"_id\":\"6ae45f48c3b566b041f6ca88\",\"name\":\"Xin Li\",\"hidden\":false},{\"_id\":\"6ae45f48c3b566b041f6ca89\",\"name\":\"Yinsong Liu\",\"hidden\":false},{\"_id\":\"6ae45f48c3b566b041f6ca8a\",\"name\":\"Deqian Jiang\",\"hidden\":false},{\"_id\":\"6ae45f48c3b566b041f6ca8b\",\"name\":\"Di Yin\",\"hidden\":false},{\"_id\":\"6ae45f48c3b566b041f6ca8c\",\"name\":\"Haoyu Cao\",\"hidden\":false},{\"_id\":\"6ae45f48c3b566b041f6ca8d\",\"name\":\"Xing Sun\",\"hidden\":false},{\"_id\":\"6ae45f48c3b566b041f6ca8e\",\"name\":\"Bing Liu\",\"hidden\":false},{\"_id\":\"6ae45f48c3b566b041f6ca8f\",\"name\":\"Yanqiu Qu\",\"hidden\":false},{\"_id\":\"6ae45f48c3b566b041f6ca90\",\"name\":\"Yunfei Wu\",\"hidden\":false},{\"_id\":\"6ae45f48c3b566b041f6ca91\",\"name\":\"Kun Yin\",\"hidden\":false},{\"_id\":\"6ae45f48c3b566b041f6ca92\",\"name\":\"Zhixiang Wei\",\"hidden\":false},{\"_id\":\"6ae45f48c3b566b041f6ca93\",\"name\":\"Yongxiang Hua\",\"hidden\":false},{\"_id\":\"6ae45f48c3b566b041f6ca94\",\"name\":\"Qianyu Li\",\"hidden\":false},{\"_id\":\"6ae45f48c3b566b041f6ca95\",\"name\":\"Xiaoxing Hu\",\"hidden\":false},{\"_id\":\"6ae45f48c3b566b041f6ca96\",\"name\":\"Peiyuan Zhang\",\"hidden\":false},{\"_id\":\"6ae45f48c3b566b041f6ca97\",\"name\":\"Lijiang Li\",\"hidden\":false},{\"_id\":\"6ae45f48c3b566b041f6ca98\",\"name\":\"Dong Xu\",\"hidden\":false},{\"_id\":\"6ae45f48c3b566b041f6ca99\",\"name\":\"Zhenchuan Yang\",\"hidden\":false},{\"_id\":\"6ae45f48c3b566b041f6ca9a\",\"name\":\"Yiliang Jiang\",\"hidden\":false}],\"mediaUrls\":[\"https://cdn-uploads.huggingface.co/production/uploads/6483143902f98c3f05aff915/VIm-4Jgo39gS47WfKKPYM.png\",\"https://cdn-uploads.huggingface.co/production/uploads/6483143902f98c3f05aff915/40tq85LRUDzghmK9EH4P3.png\"],\"publishedAt\":\"2026-10-29T00:00:00.000Z\",\"submittedOnDailyAt\":\"2026-10-30T00:00:00.000Z\",\"title\":\"Youtu-Parsing-Omni: One Encoder, One Schema, All Modalities\",\"submittedOnDailyBy\":{\"_id\":\"6483143902f98c3f05aff915\",\"avatarUrl\":\"https://cdn-avatars.huggingface.co/v1/production/uploads/6483143902f98c3f05aff915/ZhWFFgrlRsQf4MXiInh5p.jpeg\",\"isPro\":true,\"fullname\":\"沈云航 Yunhang Shen\",\"user\":\"shenyunhang\",\"type\":\"user\",\"name\":\"shenyunhang\"},\"summary\":\"We present Youtu-Parsing-Omni, an omni-modal parser that converts documents, images, audio, and video into structured records grounded in space and time, providing a perception layer for agents that read, locate, and cite evidence across modalities. Its design rests on one encoder for every modality and one schema for every task. Youtu-Omni-Encoder, initialized from a pre-trained language model to strengthen text reading, encodes all modalities with shared weights in a unified space-time coordinate system, and a few fusion layers let video frames attend to concurrent audio, bringing cross-modal fusion and temporal alignment into perception itself. OmniSchema unifies the outputs of all ten parsing tasks, allowing a single self-evolving post-training procedure, OmniSchema-Aware On-Policy Distillation (OSAD), to provide a shared token-role-based objective across tasks. In each round, the model is trained on its own rollouts against token-level targets from a reference-conditioned copy of itself, which is then refreshed with the trained weights, so that the parser and its supervision co-evolve. With a single 5 B-parameter checkpoint, Youtu-Parsing-Omni achieves state-of-the-art performance on OmniDocBench v1.6 (96.96 Overall) and leads all open-weight models on OmniParsingBench (75.08 Avg.), with its advantage concentrated on audio and video. It also achieves the best overall chart-parsing score (95.02) and the highest exact chemical-fingerprint agreement among compared systems, and matches a dedicated optical-music model in character-level transcription of typeset sheet music while staying far ahead of general-purpose systems. Code and model weights are publicly available.\",\"upvotes\":67,\"discussionId\":\"6ae45f49c3b566b041f6ca9b\",\"projectPage\":\"https://github.com/TencentCloudADP/youtu-parsing/tree/main/youtu_parsing_omni\",\"ai_summary\":\"Youtu-Parsing-Omni is a unified multi-modal parser that encodes documents, images, audio, and video into structured spatiotemporal records using shared weights and cross-modal fusion, achieving state-of-the-art results across parsing benchmarks through a self-evolving on-policy distillation procedure.\",\"ai_keywords\":[\"omni-modal parser\",\"shared weights\",\"cross-modal fusion\",\"temporal alignment\",\"self-evolving post-training\",\"on-policy distillation\",\"token-level targets\"],\"ai_summary_model\":\"thinkingmachines/Inkling-Small\",\"organization\":{\"_id\":\"66543b6e420092799d2f625c\",\"name\":\"tencent\",\"fullname\":\"Tencent\",\"avatar\":\"https://cdn-avatars.huggingface.co/v1/production/uploads/5dd96eb166059660ed1ee413/Lp3m-XLpjQGwBItlvn69q.png\"}},\"canReadDatabase\":false,\"canManagePapers\":false,\"canSubmit\":false,\"hasHfLevelAccess\":false,\"upvoted\":false,\"upvoters\":[{\"_id\":\"6483143902f98c3f05aff915\",\"avatarUrl\":\"https://cdn-avatars.huggingface.co/v1/production/uploads/6483143902f98c3f05aff915/ZhWFFgrlRsQf4MXiInh5p.jpeg\",\"isPro\":true,\"fullname\":\"沈云航 Yunhang Shen\",\"user\":\"shenyunhang\",\"type\":\"user\"},{\"_id\":\"656312995475849b82c38bc4\",\"avatarUrl\":\"/avatars/216c7fd42eebb10ed74f908117ae1efd.svg\",\"isPro\":false,\"fullname\":\"zhixiangwei\",\"user\":\"zhixiangwei\",\"type\":\"user\"},{\"_id\":\"6a2da6c8ca070ee12c6e396c\",\"avatarUrl\":\"/avatars/d5adda946bf33aa6c75a4da067cc8f69.svg\",\"isPro\":false,\"fullname\":\"Joe Mama\",\"user\":\"JoeMama123123123\",\"type\":\"user\"},{\"_id\":\"6ae48ab3e925626fdc32c3c8\",\"avatarUrl\":\"https://cdn-avatars.huggingface.co/v1/production/uploads/6ae48ab3e925626fdc32c3c8/xPNzUmkJMSK68Q0AM3RBJ.jpeg\",\"isPro\":false,\"fullname\":\"MAILCOM martin\",\"user\":\"momartin\",\"type\":\"user\"},{\"_id\":\"6ae4928346b584ab91059598\",\"avatarUrl\":\"/avatars/04950869f8cf5004ff848bb456cf86a7.svg\",\"isPro\":false,\"fullname\":\"ralph PIANO\",\"user\":\"srmistphysics35\",\"type\":\"user\"},{\"_id\":\"6ae498adac14098d22bc5a3b\",\"avatarUrl\":\"https://cdn-avatars.huggingface.co/v1/production/uploads/6ae498adac14098d22bc5a3b/HaMB77_SiH7KBegwy3xv2.jpeg\",\"isPro\":false,\"fullname\":\"Margaret-Moreno\",\"user\":\"Mamoreno0322\",\"type\":\"user\"},{\"_id\":\"6ae49a17e897384844fbb3e2\",\"avatarUrl\":\"https://cdn-avatars.huggingface.co/v1/production/uploads/6ae49a17e897384844fbb3e2/rSv6B39swYMv8J75YjRyk.jpeg\",\"isPro\":false,\"fullname\":\"jason pena\",\"user\":\"justjasonpena\",\"type\":\"user\"},{\"_id\":\"6ae49bd308d59429f395ab44\",\"avatarUrl\":\"/avatars/4e9e99f208107dd85374d8daf9e404e6.svg\",\"isPro\":false,\"fullname\":\"kayla devi\",\"user\":\"ramen-kayla\",\"type\":\"user\"},{\"_id\":\"6ae49dad04a988030bbe4432\",\"avatarUrl\":\"https://cdn-avatars.huggingface.co/v1/production/uploads/6ae49dad04a988030bbe4432/6BQMGOMVp4549OZUTYkyU.jpeg\",\"isPro\":false,\"fullname\":\"pamela\",\"user\":\"pamelawheeler\",\"type\":\"user\"},{\"_id\":\"6ae4a12436e80357472559f9\",\"avatarUrl\":\"/avatars/c44ee5c582d21f1208bc2019f1a7b0c5.svg\",\"isPro\":false,\"fullname\":\"maria Mcbride\",\"user\":\"mmcbride25\",\"type\":\"user\"},{\"_id\":\"6ae4a48dbd1662d7d10843c7\",\"avatarUrl\":\"https://cdn-avatars.huggingface.co/v1/production/uploads/6ae4a48dbd1662d7d10843c7/PshQ5wEk-g55XvLUcUQ0u.jpeg\",\"isPro\":false,\"fullname\":\"M. Dixon\",\"user\":\"mcdixon1988\",\"type\":\"user\"},{\"_id\":\"6ae4a938f673f647acc1704f\",\"avatarUrl\":\"https://cdn-avatars.huggingface.co/v1/production/uploads/6ae4a938f673f647acc1704f/3VXPA2HSvsVuJT29Ts5Yz.jpeg\",\"isPro\":false,\"fullname\":\"Lawrence Lopez\",\"user\":\"lawrenceldp\",\"type\":\"user\"}],\"acceptLanguages\":[\"*\"],\"dailyPaperRank\":2,\"organization\":{\"_id\":\"66543b6e420092799d2f625c\",\"name\":\"tencent\",\"fullname\":\"Tencent\",\"avatar\":\"https://cdn-avatars.huggingface.co/v1/production/uploads/5dd96eb166059660ed1ee413/Lp3m-XLpjQGwBItlvn69q.png\"},\"query\":{}}\">      Papers     arxiv:2610.39301                              Youtu-Parsing-Omni: One Encoder, One Schema, All Modalities    Published on Oct 29     ·       Submitted by             沈云航 Yunhang Shen            on Oct 30      #2 Paper of the day          ·        Tencent                      Upvote  67                                                                               +59                           Authors:            Yunhang Shen            ,          Zhangquan Chen           ,          Xiaotian Li           ,          Zhongpeng Cai           ,          Qing Zhou           ,          Zekai Zhang           ,          Kun Zhang           ,          Zezhong Wu           ,          Jian Hu           ,          Haihan Gao           ,          Heting Gao           ,          Xin Li           ,          Yinsong Liu           ,          Deqian Jiang           ,          Di Yin           ,          Haoyu Cao           ,          Xing Sun           ,          Bing Liu           ,          Yanqiu Qu           ,          Yunfei Wu           ,          Kun Yin           ,          Zhixiang Wei                   + 8 authors       Abstract      Youtu-Parsing-Omni is a unified multi-modal parser that encodes documents, images, audio, and video into structured spatiotemporal records using shared weights and cross-modal fusion, achieving state-of-the-art results across parsing benchmarks through a self-evolving on-policy distillation procedure.       Generated by  thinkingmachines/Inkling-Small         We present Youtu-Parsing-Omni, an    omni-modal parser    that converts documents, images, audio, and video into structured records grounded in space and time, providing a perception layer for agents that read, locate, and cite evidence across modalities. Its design rests on one encoder for every modality and one schema for every task. Youtu-Omni-Encoder, initialized from a pre-trained language model to strengthen text reading, encodes all modalities with    shared weights    in a unified space-time coordinate system, and a few fusion layers let video frames attend to concurrent audio, bringing    cross-modal fusion    and    temporal alignment    into perception itself. OmniSchema unifies the outputs of all ten parsing tasks, allowing a single    self-evolving post-training    procedure, OmniSchema-Aware    On-Policy Distillation    (OSAD), to provide a shared token-role-based objective across tasks. In each round, the model is trained on its own rollouts against    token-level targets    from a reference-conditioned copy of itself, which is then refreshed with the trained weights, so that the parser and its supervision co-evolve. With a single 5 B-parameter checkpoint, Youtu-Parsing-Omni achieves state-of-the-art performance on OmniDocBench v1.6 (96.96 Overall) and leads all open-weight models on OmniParsingBench (75.08 Avg.), with its advantage concentrated on audio and video. It also achieves the best overall chart-parsing score (95.02) and the highest exact chemical-fingerprint agreement among compared systems, and matches a dedicated optical-music model in character-level transcription of typeset sheet music while staying far ahead of general-purpose systems. Code and model weights are publicly available.          View arXiv page      View PDF          Project page                   Add to collection                                                   Community                                               shenyunhang             Paper author      Paper submitter                1 day ago                                                  Youtu-Parsing-Omni  is a compact (5B) omni-modal parsing model. Given a single input — a document page, a natural image, a chart / flowchart, a geometry figure, an audio clip or an audio-visual video — it produces one structured JSON envelope that covers both  perception  (layout elements, text, tables, formulas, bounding boxes, timestamps, ASR, OCR, acoustic events, camera motion) and  cognition  (captions, narratives, reports). \n \n\t \n\t\t  \n Input \n  --task  \n  modality  /  subtype  \n Key contents \n \n\n\t\t   \n Document page \n  document  \n  image  /  document  \n layout elements with bbox, text / LaTeX / OTSL tables / Markdown charts / Mermaid flowcharts, reading order \n \n \n Natural image \n  natural_image  \n  image  /  natural_image  \n entities and text with bbox, tags, captions, global description \n \n \n Chart \n  graphics_chart  \n  image  /  document  \n one  chart  element: Markdown table, notes, caption \n \n \n Flowchart \n  graphics_flowchart  \n  image  /  document  \n one  flowchart  element: Mermaid, caption \n \n \n Geometry figure \n  graphics_geometric  \n  image  /  document  \n one  geometric  element: points, lines, arcs, shapes, geometric relations and measurements \n \n \n Audio \n  audio  \n  audio  / – \n vocal / non-vocal segments with timestamps, speakers, ASR, timbre / scene captions, acoustic events \n \n \n Natural video \n  natural_video  \n  video  /  natural_video  \n temporal segments with visual elements, actions, interactions, camera motion, audio track \n \n \n Text-rich video \n  textrich_video  \n  video  /  text_rich_video  \n segments with OCR + ASR and a Markdown  structured_report  of the whole video \n \n \n\t \n \n Highlights: \n \n  Unified schema  – one JSON envelope for seven parsing families, driven by the task prompt. \n  Omni encoder  – image, audio and interleaved audio-visual video inputs (frames + audio track) in a single model. \n  Strong results at a small size  – state-of-the-art on OmniDocBench v1.6 (96.96 Overall), best open-weight model on OmniParsingBench (75.08 Avg., second only to Gemini-3-Pro), and competitive with specialized models on chemical-structure (ChemOCR) and music-score (PDMX-Synth) recognition ( results ). \n  Easy to serve  – a vLLM plugin, pinned serving settings, task prompts and inference examples are included. \n \n     \n     \n     \n            See translation                                                     Reply                                                                                researchstudio-bot                             1 day ago                                                 This is an automated message from the  ResearchStudio  team. \n We created an interactive ResearchStudio Reel for this paper. It includes a  visual poster , a  video , and a  blog , all available for download in editable formats. \n     \n  Open the ResearchStudio Reel →  \n  Download all files from Hugging Face  \n Please give this comment a thumbs up if you find the Reel helpful! \n Want to explore or create Reels for more papers? Visit the  ResearchStudio demo . \n            See translation                                                     Reply                                                                                librarian-bot                             about 20 hours ago                                                 This is an automated message from the  Librarian Bot . I found the following papers similar to this paper.  \n The following papers were recommended by the Semantic Scholar API  \n \n  OmniReasoning: Pushing the Limits of Audio-Visual Joint Reasoning  (2026) \n  Qwen3.8-Omni: Towards Native Omni-Modal Agents  (2026) \n  DreamX-Creator: Democratizing Native Audio-Video Generation at 2K Resolution  (2026) \n  Omni-Embed-Mini: Binding Modalities Without Forgetting via Dense Distillation  (2026) \n  AVC-Reward: Event-Centric Audio-Video Consistency Evaluation  (2026) \n  Ovis-Embedding: Pushing the Frontiers of Universal Omni-Modal Embeddings  (2026) \n  EmbeddingGemma 2: Unified and Efficient Multimodal Representations  (2026) \n \n  Please give a thumbs up to this comment if you found it helpful! \n  If you want recommendations for any Paper on Hugging Face checkout  this  Space \n  You can directly ask Librarian Bot for paper recommendations by tagging it in a comment:  @librarian-bot recommend  \n            See translation                                                     Reply                                                 Edit  Preview                                    Upload images, audio, and videos by dragging in the text input, pasting, or  clicking here .   Tap or paste here to upload images                              Comment     ·   Sign up  or  log in  to comment                           Upvote  67                                                                                                           +55                                Models citing this paper  1                      tencent/Youtu-Parsing-Omni                 Image-Text-to-Text  •        5B   •     Updated  1 day ago        •     3.05k         •      122                        Datasets citing this paper  0      No dataset linking this paper    Cite arxiv.org/abs/2610.39301 in a dataset README.md to link it from this page.       Spaces citing this paper  2           📄    tardellirs/paper-pulse           📑    mrfakename/youtu-parsing-omni                              Collections including this paper  1           Youtu      Collection        14 items   •   Updated  1 day ago     •      31                                                                     System theme                  Company   TOS   Privacy   About   Careers  