c grating using Meep. The starter submission and scientific\nenvironment are agent-facing during a controlled trial, whereas the tests,\nrubric, judge prompt, and reference artifacts remain in the evaluator\nenvironment. All components are available for inspection. \n \n \n   ⬇  \n  gmr  -  grating  -  fano  -  meep  / \n \n  |--     task  .  toml \n \n  |--     instruction  .  md \n \n  |--     environment  / \n \n  |       |--     Dockerfile \n \n  |       |--     docker  -  compose  .  yaml \n \n  |       |--     init  -  workspace  .  sh \n \n  |       |--     starter_submission  / \n \n  |       |       |--     README  .  md \n \n  |       |       |--     reproduce  .  sh \n \n  |       |       ‘--     src  / \n \n  |       ‘--     paper  / \n \n  |           |--     paper  .  md \n \n  |           |--     paper  .  pdf \n \n  |           |--     addendum  .  md \n \n  |           ‘--     paper_image  / \n \n  ‘--     tests  / \n \n        |--     test  .  sh \n \n        |--     evaluate  .  py \n \n        |--     rubric  .  json \n \n        |--     config  / \n \n        |       |--     judge_prompt  .  md \n \n        |       ‘--     public_contract  .  md \n \n        |--     refs  / \n \n        ‘--     src  / \n \n \n \n \n Components and evaluation-time visibility. \n\n \n Table   A1   separates the materials available to an\nagent from evaluator-only resources. This boundary applies during evaluation;\nthe complete demonstration package, including its evaluator resources, is now\npublic for audit. \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n Component \n  \n \n \n Role \n  \n Agent \n Evaluator  \n \n \n \n \n \n Paper and addendum \n  \n \n \n Scientific scope, measurements, and evidence requirements \n  \n  ✓  \n  ✓   \n \n \n \n Instruction \n  \n \n \n Goal, deliverables, and submission interface \n  \n  ✓  \n  ✓   \n \n \n \n Environment \n  \n \n \n Simulator, dependencies, and resource envelope \n  \n  ✓  \n  ✓   \n \n \n \n Starter submission \n  \n \n \n Editable source tree and replay entry point \n  \n  ✓  \n  ✓   \n \n \n \n Rubric \n  \n \n \n Hierarchical, independently scored scientific requirements \n  \n  ✗  \n  ✓   \n \n \n \n Judge prompt \n  \n \n \n Evidence-inspection and decision rules \n  \n  ✗  \n  ✓   \n \n \n \n Reference artifacts \n  \n \n \n Expert-generated logs, arrays, and validation records \n  \n  ✗  \n  ✓   \n \n \n  Table A1:  Task components and their visibility during evaluation. Evaluator-only\ncomponents are included in the public demonstration package after evaluation. \n \n \n \n Worked scientific contract. \n\n \n Table   A2   summarizes the parts of the GMR task that determine\nwhat must be executed and what evidence must be retained. The complete protocol\nremains authoritative; this summary illustrates its structure rather than\nreplacing it. \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n Field \n  \n \n \n Public contract \n   \n \n \n \n \n \n Scientific target \n  \n \n \n Guided-mode resonances of a three-pair multilayer dielectric grating in Meep \n   \n \n \n \n Cases \n  \n \n \n Unetched control plus full-depth air-slot widths of 0.030, 0.050, 0.070, and 0.150    μ  \\mu   m \n   \n \n \n \n Required evidence \n  \n \n \n Native spectra and logs, matched reference/device fluxes, complex reflected amplitudes, resonance fits, independent decay modes, and refinement records \n   \n \n \n \n Replay interface \n  \n \n \n No-argument  bash/home/submission/reproduce.sh , executed offline \n   \n \n \n \n Compute envelope \n  \n \n \n Meep 1.17.1, 8 CPUs, 32 GiB RAM; 7 hours for the agent, 5 hours for native calculation, and 6 hours for replay and review \n   \n \n \n \n Failure reporting \n  \n \n \n Missing, dark, overlapping, or non-identifiable features remain unresolved and cannot be replaced with paper values or invented poles \n   \n \n \n  Table A2:  Condensed public contract for the GMR demonstration task. \n \n \n \n From contract to evidence leaves. \n\n \n The hidden rubric used during evaluation converts the public scientific\nrequirements into independent leaves. Representative leaves check whether\n(i) the executed geometry contains the specified six layers and full-depth air\nslots (Modeling), (ii) clean replay regenerates genuine Meep runs, raw arrays,\nlogs, and refinement controls (Execution), and (iii) power closure, pole fits,\nmode agreement, and convergence satisfy the disclosed scientific conditions\n(Validation). A missing item affects the leaves that depend on it rather than\nsilently imposing a global zero. \n \n \n \n Evaluator policy. \n\n \n Only evidence regenerated by clean replay is admissible. The evaluator accepts\nequivalent documented data layouts and unit conversions, but does not infer\nmissing units, phase, provenance, or scientific quantities from a report.\nScientific failures receive zero on the affected leaves; evaluator read or tool\nfailures instead withhold the judgment for repair and re-evaluation. Each leaf\nis judged against its stated requirement without targeting a model-level score. \n \n \n \n Complete public record. \n\n \n The pinned   06-gmr-grating-fano-meep   directory contains the full\nagent instruction, scientific addendum, environment definition, judge prompt,\nrubric, and reference materials. \n \n \n \n \n  A.2  Complete Benchmark Inventory \n\n \n Table   A3   follows the 93-task result set used for the\nreported model results. The numeric prefix identifies the\nresearch area, and “yes” marks the public demo in that area. \n \n \n  Table A3:  Complete 93-task benchmark inventory used in the reported evaluation. \n \n \n \n \n \n ID \n  \n \n \n Task \n  \n \n \n Public demo \n   \n \n \n \n  01 RF antennas and arrays   \n \n \n \n 1-1 \n  \n \n \n  5g-smartphone-eight-element-mimo  \n  \n   \n \n \n \n 1-2 \n  \n \n \n  cpw-quad-port-uwb-mimo  \n  \n \n \n yes \n   \n \n \n \n 1-3 \n  \n \n \n  dual-band-wlan-miniaturized-patch  \n  \n   \n \n \n \n 1-4 \n  \n \n \n  f-stub-uwb-mimo  \n  \n   \n \n \n \n